         <!--dulcis et innoces hic dormit Severianus ((monogramma Christi)) in somnio pacis / qui vixit annus p(lus) m(inus) L cuius spiritus in luce domini suscep/tus est ((monogramma Christi in crucem translatum)) die VIIIX k(a)l(endas) mart(ias) dd(ominis) nn(ostris) Flavio Caesario et Nonio Attico / vv(iris) c(larissimis) c(on)s(ulibu)s quem locum emit Viricunda ux{x}or Pascasio EPC / ((avis cum olea in rostro)) ((monogramma Christi in crucem translatum in corona))--><div type="edition" xml:lang="la"><head>Text</head><ab><lb n="1"/>dulcis et innoces hic dormit Severianus <g type="descriptive">monogramma Christi</g> in somnio pacis<lb n="2"/>qui vixit annus <expan><abbr>p</abbr><ex>lus</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>m</abbr><ex>inus</ex></expan> L cuius spiritus in luce domini suscep<lb break="no" n="3"/>tus est <g type="descriptive">monogramma Christi in crucem translatum</g> die VIIIX k<expan><ex>a</ex><abbr>l</abbr><ex>endas</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>mart</abbr><ex>ias</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>dd</abbr><ex>ominis</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>nn</abbr><ex>ostris</ex></expan> Flavio Caesario et Nonio Attico<lb n="4"/><expan><abbr>vv</abbr><ex>iris</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>c</abbr><ex>larissimis</ex></expan> c<expan><ex>on</ex><abbr>s</abbr><ex>ulibu</ex><abbr>s</abbr></expan> quem locum emit Viricunda ux<surplus>x</surplus>or Pascasio EPC<lb n="5"/><g type="descriptive">avis cum olea in rostro</g> ((monogramma Christi in crucem translatum in corona))</ab></div>
         <div type="apparatus">
            <p>4ex. Silvagni writes: "intelligendum 'Pascasio ep(i)s(copo sedente, vel concedente, cel iubente)'. But "Pascasius episc. Romanus non exstitit" (Diehl, in  ILCV ad loc. cit. (Felle)</p>
